---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { resolvePath } from '../../lib/paths';
import LightningProcessAnimation from '../../components/project/LightningProcessAnimation.astro';
import LightningZoningDiagram from '../../components/project/LightningZoningDiagram.astro';
import '../../styles/project.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Background · Project"
  description="Aircraft lightning protection 101: attachment physics, swept strokes, and aerospace lightning zoning."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 pb-24">

    <!-- ===== Navigation Breadcrumb ===== -->
    <nav class="mb-10" aria-label="Breadcrumb" data-reveal="1">
      <a
        href={resolvePath('/project')}
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-solar hover:text-solar-light transition-colors"
        style="border-bottom:none;"
      >
        <span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Back to Project Timeline
      </a>
    </nav>

    <!-- ===== Header ===== -->
    <header class="project-detail-header" data-reveal="1">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-display font-bold leading-[1.25] pb-3 mb-2">
        Project Background
      </h1>

      <p class="text-solar-light text-xl font-sans font-light max-w-3xl leading-relaxed mb-3">
        Aircraft Lightning Protection 101
      </p>

      <time class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-void-400 block">
        February 2025
      </time>
    </header>

    <!-- ===== Content Sections ===== -->
    <article class="space-y-16 mt-10" data-reveal="2">

      <!-- =========================================================================
           Section 1: When Lightning Strikes
           ========================================================================= -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-display font-bold text-void-100 mb-4">
          1. When Lightning Strikes
        </h2>

        <!-- Verbatim intro -->
        <p class="text-void-200 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Aircraft lightning strikes are probably more frequent than you'd expect, but thankfully modern aircraft are well-protected against catastrophic lightning damage.
        </p>

        <!-- Statistics Boxes -->
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 my-8">
          <div class="border border-solar/20 bg-void-950 p-4 relative overflow-hidden">
            <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--tl"></div>
            <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--tr"></div>
            <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--bl"></div>
            <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--br"></div>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-solar block mb-1">01 / STRIKE FREQUENCY</span>
            <span class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white block">~1 / yr</span>
            <p class="text-void-400 text-xs mt-2 mb-0">per commercial aircraft</p>
          </div>

          <div class="border border-solar/20 bg-void-950 p-4 relative overflow-hidden">
            <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--tl"></div>
            <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--tr"></div>
            <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--bl"></div>
            <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--br"></div>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-solar block mb-1">02 / AIRCRAFT TRIGGERED</span>
            <span class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white block">~90%</span>
            <p class="text-void-400 text-xs mt-2 mb-0">Strikes triggered by the presence of the aircraft</p>
          </div>

          <div class="border border-solar/20 bg-void-950 p-4 relative overflow-hidden">
            <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--tl"></div>
            <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--tr"></div>
            <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--bl"></div>
            <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--br"></div>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-solar block mb-1">03 / RISK</span>
            <span class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white block">10<sup>-9</sup> / flt hr</span>
            <p class="text-void-400 text-xs mt-2 mb-0">Probability of catastrophic failure due to lightning</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Interactive Physics Animation of the Strike Process -->
        <LightningProcessAnimation />

        <!-- Damage Categorization Boxes -->
        <div class="mt-8">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs text-solar uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold mb-3">
            Damage Classification // Direct vs. Indirect
          </div>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <div class="border border-solar/20 bg-void-950 p-5 relative overflow-hidden">
              <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--tl"></div>
              <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--tr"></div>
              <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--bl"></div>
              <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--br"></div>
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-solar block mb-1">01 / DIRECT EFFECTS</span>
              <span class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white block mb-2">Physical Damage</span>
              <p class="text-void-300 text-sm font-sans mb-0 leading-relaxed">
                <strong>Burning, pitting, melting</strong>, acoustic shockwaves, and composite delamination occurring immediately at lightning arc attachment points.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="border border-solar/20 bg-void-950 p-5 relative overflow-hidden">
              <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--tl"></div>
              <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--tr"></div>
              <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--bl"></div>
              <div class="card-hud-corner card-hud-corner--br"></div>
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-solar block mb-1">02 / INDIRECT EFFECTS</span>
              <span class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white block mb-2">Electromagnetic Damage</span>
              <p class="text-void-300 text-sm font-sans mb-0 leading-relaxed">
                <strong>Electromagnetic interference and computer failure</strong> induced by severe transient magnetic fields and currents coupling into onboard wiring harnesses and avionics.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =========================================================================
           Section 2: Lightning Zoning
           ========================================================================= -->
      <section class="pt-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-display font-bold text-void-100 mb-4">
          2. Lightning Zoning
        </h2>

        <!-- Verbatim intro -->
        <p class="text-void-200 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
          The first stage in aircraft lightning protection is zoning. We divide the aircraft into 3 zones (6 sub-zones) based on the localized lightning risk.
        </p>

        <!-- Aircraft Zoning Illustration & Detail View -->
        <LightningZoningDiagram />

        <!-- Key Industry Comment Callout -->
        <div class="project-callout my-8">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-xs font-bold text-solar uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-solar" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
            </svg>
            <span>Key Takeaway // Certification &amp; Future Aircraft</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-void-200 text-sm md:text-base font-sans italic leading-relaxed mb-0">
            "We usually zone 'tube and wing' aircraft by 'similarity', which means looking at an existing aircraft with in-service experience and making the zoning about the same. This is often over-conservative, and won't work for next-generation aircraft with unconventional shapes."
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =========================================================================
           Section 3: Simulation Methods
           ========================================================================= -->
      <section class="opacity-50 border-t border-solar/15 pt-8 mt-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-display font-bold text-void-200 mb-2">
          3. Simulation Methods
        </h2>
      </section>

      <!-- =========================================================================
           Section 4: The Challenge
           ========================================================================= -->
      <section class="opacity-50 border-t border-solar/15 pt-8 mt-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-display font-bold text-void-200 mb-2">
          4. The Challenge
        </h2>
      </section>

    </article>

    <!-- ===== Navigation to Next Milestone ===== -->
    <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-solar/20" data-reveal="4">
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href={resolvePath('/project')} class="project-nav-adjacent">
          <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-void-400">Timeline</span>
          <span class="font-sans font-medium text-void-200 mt-1">← Return to All Milestones</span>
        </a>

        <a href={resolvePath('/project/proposal')} class="project-nav-adjacent text-right">
          <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-solar">Next Milestone // 02</span>
          <span class="font-sans font-medium text-solar-light mt-1">Project Proposal →</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
